, "last_played": 1684879388, "avatar": "37dc51900c38c9a127db9674a103fa9fc5ecbc42"}, "language": "english", "review": "The number is inaccurate as Steam does not track my modded hours. I have over 150 hours. Some of my runs are on YouTube.\n9/10 Art\n10/10 Soundtrack\n10/10 Gameplay\n9/10 Performance\n10/10 Fun\n10/10 Glitches\n8/10 Progression\n10/10 Atmosphere\n10/10 Replayability\n10/10 Bias\n\n96/100\nArt is beautiful and sometimes simple pixel art. Everything has so much character.\nSoundtrack is extremely well done. It sounds alien and powerful. Which so happens to match the theme!\nGameplay is like other rouges but more number and stacking based. There is not much synergies but still there are some survivors with better compatibilities. \nPerformance is fine. Late into games(2+hours) it can get a bit slow.\nFUN! It is very fun. The gameplay loop is fun and so are the characters to play. \nGlitches. Few impactful glitches when not playing modded.\nProgression, Acheivements directely unlock new items and survivors. Its a good progress system that encourages unlocking acheivements and trying new playstyles.\nAtmosphere, The soundtrack, lore logs, and small scale of the player make the atmosphere intense. It truly does feel as though you are an alien invader on this planet that hates you.\nReplayability, Three difficulties, twelve characters, and 10 gamechanging artifacts. So, there is a lot of replayability. Not even counting the wonderful mods that add hundreds of everything more.\nBias, I like rouges and this game has a space horror theme. I like that.\nOverall good atmospheric rouge game with tons of replayability!", "timestamp_created": 1668127071, "timestamp_updated": 1668127146, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1383930480", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 21, "count": 1}]}]}